  "query_preview": "..\nToday and tonight: An upper low dropping in from Alberta/Sask has\nbrought another push of colder air with strong NW winds this \nafternoon. Wind chills at noon ranged from near 10 across the \nnorth to the teens to near 20 south. Winds are expected to drop \noff later today but temps tonight are expected to drop into the \nteens most places, the coldest night this season for most areas \n(coldest temp this year so for Glasgow has been 21, which occurred\nthis morning).\n\nTomorrow (Sunday) will feature a cold start, and with light winds\nand little mixing, temps are only expected to reach the mid 20s to\naround 30, about 5 to 15 degrees below normal.\n\nMonday, with the upper low moving out, temps should begin to\nrebound. A large upper low over the Gulf of Alaska will also help\nto set up a zonal flow over Montana this week, allowing milder air\nto flow in. It looks to be mainly dry this week but there could be\na brief shower about Friday. Friday looks to be the warmest day\nthis week with highs in the 40s to near 50.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThe only deviation made to NBM were to raise pops toward GFS &\nConsShort to account for the flurries/snow showers through early\nthis evening.\n\n- High confidence(60-90%) through Monday night. \n\n- Moderate confidence(40-60%) in the forecast from Tuesday to \n  Wednesday night.\n\n- Low confidence (15-25%) Thursday onward.  \n\nTFJ",
